%In one sample simulation, the method reconstructed the estimated biases at the visited positions with a root mean square error (RMSE) of $0.2786m$. As process noise ranges from $0m$ to $0.5m$, the SBE's final RMSE grows proportionally to the noise. After passing these outputs to a Gaussian process model, we construct the estimated bias function across the environment, yielding an RMSE of $1.0569m$. In a separate setup that incorporates IPP, we demonstrate the improvement of the estimated bias function's RMSE from an initial $2.1605m$ at 2 seconds of runtime, to an RMSE of $1.1748m$ after 20 seconds of runtime.
