Additionally, we also present a flexible, scalable deployment architecture and answer the question: \emph{Will your WiFi’s sensing function crash your video call?} We examine how WiFi sensing and data communication interact under standard WiFi protocols—critical considerations for managing bandwidth, latency, and interference. 

Despite these hurdles, our large-scale deployment demonstrates that robust WiFi-based home monitoring is both achievable and beneficial. Our prototype system demonstrated a 92.61\% human motion detection rate across 15 homes in 11 U.S. states on 280 existing IoT devices in real-world testing. By detailing our successful experiences, we provide practical guidance on overcoming these challenges and offer insights into designing, building, and integrating WiFi sensing solutions into actual homes. 
Although we primarily focus on home monitoring, the methods and experiences shared here extend to various WiFi-based applications, from health monitoring to smart buildings. 
Ultimately, our work paves the way for more widespread adoption of WiFi sensing technologies, shaping the world into a smarter, safer living space. 

