% See \Cref{app:act_schd_pf}.
% \end{proof}

\Cref{thm:Act_sch_guarantee} shows that the cost function evaluated at the output of \Cref{alg:greedy_algo_epsilon} is upper bounded by a convex combination of $\trace{\matW_{\calG_0}^{-1}}$ and $E^*$. 
%Note that both the terms on the right-hand side of \eqref{eq:Act_sch_guarantee_2} depend on the initial schedule $\calG_0$. 
%For the same reason that $\trace{\matW_\calG^{-1}} \leq \trace{\matW_{\calG_0}}$, $E^* \leq \trace{\matW_{\calG_0}^{-1}}$. 
Therefore, to minimize this bound, we next discuss how to choose $\calG_0$ leveraging \Cref{alg:LI_Schedule_FullB}. %, which in turn reduces the average energy even further.
%Recall that $\calG_0$ is the output of \Cref{alg:LI_Schedule_FullB}. 
