    Suppose there exist two schedules $\tilde{\calS}, \hat{\calS} \in \Phi$ such that $\rank{\matW_{\tilde{\calS}}}=R$ and $\rank{\matW_{\hat{\calS}}}=R+1$. Then, there exists $\epsilon^*>0$ such that for any $\epsilon<\epsilon^*$, the greedy algorithm chooses $\hat{\calS}$ over $\tilde{\calS}$.% and $\hat{\calS}$.
