We will now discuss the semantics of programs $C\in\cmd$ as pomsets, which record both the causality between atomic actions and the branching behavior of tests. The label set $\lab \triangleq \act \cup \test \cup \{ \fork, \bot\}$ consists of actions, tests, fork, and bottom nodes, which forms a pointed \dcpo, with $\bot$ as the bottom. Actions are ordered according to $\le_\act$; for any other label $\ell \in \test \cup \{\fork\}$, we only have $\bot \le \ell$ and $\ell \le\ell$. We will also henceforth use $\pom \triangleq \pom(\lab)$ to refer to pomsets over this label set.
